#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:182
msgid ""
"この計算ではどちらの見かけの転移温度も上がった。有限セルでは、新しい相の 核が生まれる体積と、成長できるサイズがともに変わる。大きいセルで核を作る"
" 場所が増えると転移は早まりうる。逆に、小セルで単位胞がそろって変形する経路が "
"選ばれていた場合、セルを広げると変形の進み方も変わる。表の増加幅だけで、 どの要因が支配したかを特定することは難しい。"
msgstr ""
"Both apparent transition temperatures rose in this simulation. In a "
"finite cell, the available volume for nucleation of the new phase and the"
" size to which it can grow both change. A larger cell can make the "
"transition occur sooner if it provides more sites for nucleation. "
"Conversely, if the small cell favored a pathway in which unit cells "
"deform in concert, enlarging the cell also changes how the deformation "
"proceeds. The increases in the table alone make it difficult to identify "
"which factor dominated."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:191
msgid "説明用の事例：加熱と冷却で現れる温度差"
msgstr "Worked Example: Temperature Difference Between Heating and Cooling"

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:193
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"構造が温度の変化に追いつかない場合、加熱と冷却で同じ判定基準を使っても 転移温度に差が出る。単純な模型として、規格化した秩序変数 "
":math:`Q` の 平衡値 :math:`Q_{\\rm eq}` が、温度 :math:`T_0=400\\,\\mathrm{K}` "
"の上下で 低温側の1と高温側の0に切り替わるとする。緩和の時間尺度を :math:`\\tau=4\\,\\mathrm{ps}` "
"とおき、変化の速さが平衡値からのずれに比例する と仮定する。"
msgstr ""
"If the structure cannot keep up with the changing temperature, heating "
"and cooling give different transition temperatures even with the same "
"criterion. In a simple model, take a normalized order parameter :math:`Q`"
" whose equilibrium value :math:`Q_{\\rm eq}` is 1 below "
":math:`T_0=400\\,\\mathrm{K}` and 0 above it. Set the relaxation "
"timescale to :math:`\\tau=4\\,\\mathrm{ps}` and assume the rate of change"
" is proportional to the deviation from equilibrium:"

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:200
msgid ""
"\\frac{dQ}{dt}=\\frac{Q_{\\rm eq}-Q}{\\tau},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Q(t)-Q_{\\rm eq}=[Q(0)-Q_{\\rm eq}]\\exp(-t/\\tau)."
msgstr ""
"\\frac{dQ}{dt}=\\frac{Q_{\\rm eq}-Q}{\\tau},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"Q(t)-Q_{\\rm eq}=[Q(0)-Q_{\\rm eq}]\\exp(-t/\\tau)."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:207
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"右の式は、設定温度が :math:`T_0` を通過した時刻を :math:`t=0` とし、 通過後の :math:`Q_{\\rm eq}` "
"を一定に保った場合の解である。加熱では :math:`Q` が1から下がり、冷却では0から上がる。両方の軌跡で :math:`Q=1/2` "
"を転移と判定すると、遅れは :math:`\\tau\\ln 2=2.773\\,\\mathrm{ps}` となる。"
msgstr ""
"The expression on the right is the solution obtained by taking the "
"crossing of :math:`T_0` by the set temperature as :math:`t=0` and holding"
" :math:`Q_{\\rm eq}` constant after the crossing. During heating, "
":math:`Q` falls from 1, and during cooling it rises from 0. Using "
":math:`Q=1/2` as the transition criterion for both trajectories gives a "
"delay of :math:`\\tau\\ln 2=2.773\\,\\mathrm{ps}`."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:213
msgid ""
"加熱・冷却の速さをともに10 K/psとすると、温度のずれは片側で約27.7 Kである。 :numref:`fig-heat-order-"
"lag`\\ の丸印では、加熱で427.7 K、冷却で372.3 Kになる。 この模型のヒステリシス幅は丸め前の値から求めると55.5 Kである。"
msgstr ""
"At heating and cooling rates of 10 K/ps, the temperature shift is about "
"27.7 K on each side. The circles in :numref:`fig-heat-order-lag`\\  mark "
"427.7 K during heating and 372.3 K during cooling. The model's hysteresis"
" width is 55.5 K when calculated from the unrounded values."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:217
msgid "加熱では秩序変数が400 Kより上で0.5に達し、冷却では400 Kより下で0.5に達する。"
msgstr ""
"The order parameter reaches 0.5 above 400 K during heating and below 400 "
"K during cooling."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:222
msgid "緩和の遅れを表す模型の秩序変数。実線は加熱、破線は冷却。 点線は模型の平衡境界400 Kと判定値0.5、丸印は見かけの転移温度を表す。"
msgstr ""
"Order parameter in a model of delayed relaxation. The solid line shows "
"heating, and the dashed line shows cooling. The dotted lines mark the "
"model equilibrium boundary at 400 K and the threshold of 0.5. The circles"
" mark the apparent transition temperatures."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:228
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:230
msgid ""
"**軌跡上の判定と平衡。** 秩序変数の急変は、その軌跡が別の構造へ移った時刻を "
"示す。平衡境界を知るには、各温度で十分に緩和させた分布や二相の自由エネルギー "
"を求める必要がある。加熱と冷却の遅れが対称になるのは、この模型の仮定による。 "
"核形成や成長が異なる速度で起きる系では、両方向で遅れの大きさも変わる。"
msgstr ""
"**Trajectory-based criteria and equilibrium.** An abrupt change in the "
"order parameter shows when the trajectory switched to a different "
"structure. Finding the equilibrium boundary requires either distributions"
" after sufficient relaxation at each temperature or the free energy of "
"each phase. The symmetry of the heating and cooling delays follows from "
"the assumptions of this model. In systems where nucleation or growth "
"proceeds at different rates in the two directions, the delays also differ"
" in magnitude."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:234
msgid ""
"**変位分布の温度幅。** 軌跡を温度帯で区切って分布を作るときは、転移を "
"またぐと二つの相のフレームが一つの分布に混ざる。温度帯を細かくすると両相を 分けやすくなるが、帯ごとのフレームも少なくなる。 "
"ピークの位置や向きが平均幅に敏感なら、平滑化の違いを相の差と誤認しないよう、 独立な軌跡や一定温度での保持から分布を補う。"
msgstr ""
"**Temperature windows for displacement distributions.** When binning "
"trajectory frames by temperature, a window that straddles the transition "
"mixes frames from both phases in a single distribution. Narrower windows "
"make it easier to separate the phases but leave fewer frames in each "
"window. If the peak positions or orientations are sensitive to the "
"averaging window, supplement the distributions with data from independent"
" trajectories or holds at constant temperature to avoid mistaking a "
"smoothing effect for a phase difference."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:239
msgid ""
"**セルサイズとばらつき。** 一つのサイズにつき一つの軌跡だけを比べると、 "
"構造が切り替わる時刻の偶然のばらつきもサイズ差に含まれる。初速度を変えた "
"複数の軌跡で判定温度の分布を求めれば、そのばらつきとサイズの効果を区別できる。"
msgstr ""
"**Cell size and scatter.** Comparing only one trajectory per cell size "
"folds random variation in when the structure switches into the apparent "
"difference between sizes. Distributions of the detected transition "
"temperatures from multiple trajectories with different initial velocities"
" help distinguish that variation from the effect of cell size."

#: ../../md/heating_simulation.rst:242
msgid ""
"**相の判定と融解。** 多くの分域がある場合、全体の分極が打ち消し合うことがある。 "
"結晶相を判定するときは変位分布と格子を照合する。融解では結合配向だけでなく :ref:`拡散<mean-squared-"
"displacement>`\\ も見ると、秩序が弱くなった固体と流動する液体を区別する根拠が増える。"
msgstr ""
"**Phase identification and melting.** When there are many domains, their "
"polarizations may cancel in the overall average. To identify the crystal "
"phase, compare the displacement distribution with the lattice. When "
"testing for melting, examining :ref:`diffusion <mean-squared-"
"displacement>`\\  alongside bond orientation provides more evidence for "
"distinguishing a solid with reduced order from a flowing liquid."

